  "verification_note": "PMC3831637 is a modeling paper on P. denitrificans denitrification; it does NOT contain the defined medium's salts, buffer, vitamins, trace-element list, or carbon source with amounts (these are only cited from Felgate et al. 2012). The medium is carbon-LIMITED; the paper does not name succinate, so the current record's 'succinate carbon source' cannot be verified from this source. Full formulatio",
  "recipe_evidence": "Gaimster et al. 2016 (reproducing the Felgate et al. 2012 medium): defined minimal medium contained '29 mmol/L Na2HPO4, 11 mmol/L KH2PO4, 10 mmol/L NH4Cl, 0.4 mmol/L MgSO4' supplemented with '30 mmol/L sodium succinate, 20 mmol/L NaNO3' and 2 mL/L Vishniac and Santer trace elements solution ['130 mmol/L EDTA, 7.64 mmol/L ZnSO4, 25 mmol/L MnCl2, 18.5 mmol/L FeSO4, 0.89 mmol/L (NH4)6Mo7O24, 6.4 mmol/L CuSO4, 6.72 mmol/L CoCl2, 37.4 mmol/L CaCl2']. Trace-element final concentrations above are the stock values diluted 2 mL/L. PMC3831637 (Woolfenden et al. 2013) models exactly this system (Paracocc",
  "recipe_confidence": "high",
  "base_medium": "Paracoccus denitrificans defined minimal chemostat medium (succinate carbon / nitrate electron acceptor), phosphate-buffered, with 2 mL/L Vishniac & Santer trace-element solution; anaerobic denitrifying chemostat, D=0.05 h-1. High-copper variant ([Cu]~13 umol/L, full CuSO4 in trace mix).",
  "base_medium_reference": "Felgate H., Giannopoulos G., Sullivan M.J., Gates A.J., Clarke T.A., Baggs E., Rowley G., Richardson D.J. (2012) 'The impact of copper, nitrate and carbon status on the emission of nitrous oxide by two species of bacteria with biochemically distinct denitrification pathways.' Environmental Microbiology 14(7):1788-1800. PMID: 22642644, DOI: 10.1111/j.1462-2920.2012.02789.x. Full composition reproduced verbatim in Gaimster et al. 2016 Front. Microbiol. 7:1806 (DOI 10.3389/fmicb.2016.01806) and following Sullivan et al. 2013.",
  "verification_evidence": "the defined minimal medium contained 29 mmol/L Na2HPO4, 11 mmol/L KH2PO4, 10 mmol/L NH4Cl, 0.4 mmol/L MgSO4",
